*.log
*.nc
!NSe/Bathymetry/bathymetry_nse.nc
*.prof
*.prof.stats
__pycache__
reorganise_meteo.sh

# Generated validation outputs — sync via rsync/manage-analyses, not git
# analyses/ itself is NOT ignored — it contains hand-authored markdown.
# analyses/.gitignore handles selective ignoring of generated subdirs.
/validation-data/

# driver/oceanicu_driver.py --dump-python's default output filename (and
# NSe/config/'s own, for the real nse_from_oceanicu.yaml output) -- a
# one-off standalone debugging script (see pygetm_config.codegen's own
# docstring), regenerated on demand, not meant to be committed. Includes its
# companion config YAML (TODO item 10 -- config_yaml_path) and, since TODO
# item 35 (pygetm-config), its companion "_utils.py" module.
driver/generated*.py
driver/generated*_config.yaml
NSe/config/generated*.py
NSe/config/generated*_config.yaml

# driver/dist/schema.json -- a build artifact (pygetm-config dump output,
# with PYGETM_CONFIG_PROVIDERS pointed at oceanicu_providers.py so it
# includes hydrography/boundaries.*/river_discharge/meteo too, not just core
# pygetm-config sections), goes stale the moment pygetm/pygetm-config/
# oceanicu_providers.py changes -- regenerate, don't commit. Matches
# pygetm-config's own dist/ convention (also gitignored there). See
# driver/README.md for the regeneration command.
driver/dist/

# running/relay.env -- per-machine OCEANICU_EXPERIMENT_DB/OCEANICU_RELAY_DIR
# values (see running/relay.env.example, which IS committed, and
# running/EXPERIMENT_TRACKING.md's "Working across machines" section). Not
# secret by itself, just genuinely per-machine -- nothing to gain from
# committing one machine's copy as if it were canonical.
running/relay.env

# /experiments/ -- the real experiment tree some machines point
# OCEANICU_EXPERIMENT_ROOT_BASE at directly under the repo checkout for
# convenience (see setup_experiment_tracking.sh workstation). Ignore
# everything under it EXCEPT the small staged driver/config files
# (generated*.py/generated*.yaml -- same whitelist `stage`/
# pull_experiment_files.sh already use, oceanicu_experiments.py's own
# _STAGE_DEFAULT_INCLUDES -- currently a few 100 KB total, worth having
# on GitHub) -- once running, chunk output/logs/restarts land in this
# same tree too and CAN be multi-GB/TB (see /work/shared/oceanICU/ on
# production, a genuinely separate mount for exactly that data on those
# machines -- but nothing stops OCEANICU_EXPERIMENT_ROOT_BASE from
# pointing here on some other machine), so this stays a narrow allow-
# list, not a blanket un-ignore. The `**/` un-ignore is required for git
# to even descend into subdirectories to check the file-level rules
# below it -- a bare `/experiments/` (no wildcard) ignore, like this
# used to be, blocks descending entirely, so per-file negation
# patterns wouldn't work without it.
/experiments/**
!/experiments/**/
!/experiments/**/generated*.py
!/experiments/**/generated*.yaml
